    "body": "> Mirrored from the Solorion Tracker — **TRK-0183** is the source of truth. Edits here do not flow back.\n\nDurable fix for Cooper GitHub access while cooper-the-fox is suspended (and after): build an org-owned GitHub App (Option A in the plan) - org owns the app, installed on a selected repo set, permissions Contents/Pull requests/Issues RW + org Projects RW, private key in Vaultwarden, 1h installation tokens minted by a script on Tritium (JWT RS256 -> /app/installations/{id}/access_tokens). Runs all bulk/scheduled GitHub work (hygiene/bookkeeper/janitor crons, bounty-sync, crew sweeps) under a non-human identity with least-privilege scoping and a bot audit trail; de-risks future suspensions (no user account to ban, no authored content to hide). Option B (Muse connector Write=Allow flip) is immediate relief for directed work only - it acts as ScottyVenable, not an automation vehicle. New machine user REJECTED (circumvention exposure + same failure mode). Forgejo mirror = horizon option. Blocked on Scotty: 6 clicks listed in the plan (create app, generate key, vault it, install on org, relay App ID + Installation ID + vault item name; plus the independent connector Settings flip). Plan: ~/workspace/overnight-2026-10-18/github-access-plan.md. Related: TRK-0102 (fox appeal), TRK-0147 (bounty-sync credential), TRK-0101 (suspension).\n\n---\n**Tracker fields**\n- Kind: task · Status: planned · Priority: high\n\n<!-- tracker:TRK-0183 -->\n\n— cooper, via Quantum AI App",
